BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:state-pte-new-hampshire-2025-03-17@ustaxcalendar.com
DTSTAMP:20260924T115707Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250317
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250318
SUMMARY:New Hampshire: BT-Summary due
DESCRIPTION:New Hampshire partnership returns due the 15th day of the 3rd m
 onth after year-end\; S-corporations are treated the same as C corporations
  (15th day of the 4th month\, April 15) for Business Profits Tax purposes. 
 NH has no income tax on wages/pass-through income itself - BPT/BET apply at
  the entity level. Correction (this rebuild session): the cited source stat
 es the general rule (15th day of the 3rd month) without addressing the 2026
 -specific weekend interaction - March 15\, 2026 is a Sunday. Consistent wit
 h every other state in this data set that explicitly confirms a weekend-shi
 ft policy (e.g. Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermont\, Delaware\, Montana\, O
 regon all confirm shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, and with the near-universa
 l US government-deadline convention of shifting to the next business day\, 
 this entry's date_2026 was corrected from an unshifted March 15\, 2026 to M
 arch 16\, 2026. This is a computed application of the general shift convent
 ion\, not an independently re-fetched per-state confirmation that this spec
 ific state's statute shifts - flagged here for transparency. | New Hampshir
 e partnership returns due the 15th day of the 3rd month after year-end\; S-
 corporations are treated the same as C corporations (15th day of the 4th mo
 nth\, April 15) for Business Profits Tax purposes. NH has no income tax on 
 wages/pass-through income itself - BPT/BET apply at the entity level. File 
 Form BT-EXT for a 7-month extension (partnerships due March 15\; S-corps tr
 eated as C-corps\, due April 15). Correction (this rebuild session): the ci
 ted source states the general rule (15th day of the 3rd month) without addr
 essing the 2026-specific weekend interaction - March 15\, 2026 is a Sunday.
  Consistent with every other state in this data set that explicitly confirm
 s a weekend-shift policy (e.g. Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermont\, Delawar
 e\, Montana\, Oregon all confirm shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, and with th
 e near-universal US government-deadline convention of shifting to the next 
 business day\, this entry's date_2026 was corrected from an unshifted March
  15\, 2026 to March 16\, 2026. This is a computed application of the genera
 l shift convention\, not an independently re-fetched per-state confirmation
  that this specific state's statute shifts - flagged here for transparency.
  | Authority: New Hampshire DRA FAQ\, direct fetch this session: "partnersh
 ip returns are due on the 15th day of the 3rd month following the end of th
 e taxable period" and "Sub-S corporations are treated the same as C Corpora
 tions." The 7-month BT-EXT extension length is confirmed via a Cornell LII 
 mirror of NH Admin. Code Rev 2411.02 (NH's own revenue.nh.gov PDF returned 
 403 on every direct fetch attempt this session) rather than a live revenue.
 nh.gov page. | Source: https://www.revenue.nh.gov/resource-center/frequentl
 y-asked-questions/business-profits-tax | This date is computed from a recur
 rence rule and may not reflect a later-announced change\; confirm against t
 he cited source before relying on it.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
